IC_kwDOAO6SJc6v_hDN","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-07T15:29:04Z","updated_at":"2025-06-07T15:29:14Z","body":"Still happening on `v4.4.1.stable.mono`\n\nThe GDScript version reports a stack overflow:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/13dbc75b-733e-431f-9fee-1d304fda6a7b)\n\nSo maybe that's also what's happening from C#, and it isn't being reported properly.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2952663245/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3006045572","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99441#issuecomment-3006045572","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99441","id":3006045572,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6zLJ2E","user":{"login":"raulsntos","id":3903059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDMwNTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3903059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos","html_url":"https://github.com/raulsntos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-25T20:25:41Z","updated_at":"2025-06-25T20:25:41Z","body":"It looks like the crash is caused by calling `_start_tweeners` with a `current_step` value that goes over `tweeners.size()`. It looks like the tween finishes, and then I guess the `Tween::custom_step` API is forcing it to continue past that step limit?\n\nHere's the stack trace:\n\n```\nVectorWriteProxy<List<Ref<Tweener>, DefaultAllocator>>::operator[](long) (/godot/core/templates/vector.h:54)\nTween::_start_tweeners() (/godot/scene/animation/tween.cpp:84)\nTween::step(double) (/godot/scene/animation/tween.cpp:401)\nSceneTree::process_tweens(double, bool) (/godot/scene/main/scene_tree.cpp:822)\nSceneTree::process(double) (/godot/scene/main/scene_tree.cpp:708)\nMain::iteration() (/godot/main/main.cpp:4771)\nOS_LinuxBSD::run() (/godot/platform/linuxbsd/os_linuxbsd.cpp:989)\nmain (/godot/platform/linuxbsd/godot_linuxbsd.cpp:85)\n__libc_start_call_main (@__libc_start_call_main:29)\n__libc_start_main_impl (@__libc_start_main@@GLIBC_2.34:43)\n_start (@_start:15)\n```\n\nThe issue seems to be on this code:\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/30456ba095c425d5ecde320a96a763afb93bbcb0/scene/animation/tween.cpp#L374-L403\n\nAs I'm not familiar with this part of the codebase, it's not clear to me what the proper solution would be.\n\nMaybe we're missing `current_step = 0;` before the `_start_tweeners();` in line 401. Making this change seems to be enough to prevent the crash.\n\nAlternatively, maybe we just need to change one or both of these conditions:\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/30456ba095c425d5ecde320a96a763afb93bbcb0/scene/animation/tween.cpp#L378\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/30456ba095c425d5ecde320a96a763afb93bbcb0/scene/animation/tween.cpp#L380\n\nTo use `>=` instead of `==`.\n\ncc @KoBeWi","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3006045572/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3007910175","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99441#issuecomment-3007910175","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99441","id":3007910175,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6zSREf","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-26T09:57:33Z","updated_at":"2025-06-26T09:57:33Z","body":"I think the main issue here is that you are stepping the Tween while it's already processing. Since it happens mid-step, the Tween will repeat it infinitely, trying to call the same callback that steps it again.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3007910175/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]